## About Me

- I'm a 14-year-old developer.
- I started coding in 2025.
- I work across macOS, iOS and Linux.
- I'm interested in reverse engineering, operating systems and customization.
- My GitHub originally focused on archiving projects that might disappear. Now I mainly develop and publish my own projects.

## How I Got Started

Back in 2024, I had an iPhone 6 and discovered jailbreaking. Naturally, I ended up jailbreaking it and experimenting with tweaks and customization.

At the start of 2025, I upgraded to an iPhone 11. Suddenly, I was using a non-jailbroken iPhone, which felt pretty unusual. It wasn't a huge downside, though, since most of the tweaks I used were things like GesturesXV and other modifications that made iOS feel more modern.

For my birthday, I eventually got an iPhone X and jailbroke it. I've kept it ever since, using it for experimentation, downgrades and various iOS projects. If its Face ID still worked, I'd probably still use it over my iPhone 11.

Over time, my interests expanded beyond iOS. I started exploring macOS development, Linux, desktop customization and reverse engineering.

## What I Work On

- **macOS development** – Utilities, desktop applications and system customization.
- **iOS development & research** – Jailbreaking, tweaks, customization and legacy iOS.
- **Linux development** – CLI tools, desktop utilities, Wayland environments and system customization.
- **Reverse engineering** – Exploring operating systems, software internals and platform behaviour.
- **Random experiments** – Building unnecessarily complicated things for unnecessarily simple problems.

